{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1456810-intergalactic-travel","id":1456810,"title":"Intergalactic Travel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-14T08:55:29-07:00","id":1456810,"title":"Intergalactic Travel","content":"TC: \u00c6on says that intergalactic travel is currently not feasible. But what about satellite galaxies of the Milky Way such as the Magellanic Clouds or the Canis Major Dwarf? At least four of the Milky Way's satellites (the Sagittarius Dwarf Elliptical Galaxy, the Canis Major Dwarf, Segue 1 and Tucana III) are closer to Earth than Chrome Prime is and that world is well within Earth's capabilities to reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26999,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26999-rhiannon-vashti","user":"Rhiannon Vashti","date":". 08-14-2021, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26999-rhiannon-vashti","name":"Rhiannon Vashti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26999_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T17:50:06-07:00","id":1456843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhiannon Vashti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1456810-intergalactic-travel#post1456810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TC: \u00c6on says that intergalactic travel is currently not feasible. But what about satellite galaxies of the Milky Way such as the Magellanic Clouds or the Canis Major Dwarf? At least four of the Milky Way's satellites (the Sagittarius Dwarf Elliptical Galaxy, the Canis Major Dwarf, Segue 1 and Tucana III) are closer to Earth than Chrome Prime is and that world is well within Earth's capabilities to reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two ways of looking at this and you\u2019ll have to decide what works for your game. The first is to say \u2018sure, you can travel there, they\u2019re not that far compared to other things we do\u2019. The second is to say \u2018no, you can\u2019t go there. Psi works on not entirely understood rules of association and those galaxies aren\u2019t the Milky Way\u2019.<br /> <br /> Which works for your game?<br /> <br /> Edit: Personally, I\u2019d go with the later as a story hook for characters to explore and find the closest possible Milky Way stars to the destination galaxies, then work out ways of bridging the gap. Possibly have Aeon, the UN and various nations and psi orders work together to build a station at this point to work on solving the mystery of getting to that next (close) galaxy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 08-14-2021, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T19:24:18-07:00","id":1456924,"title":"","content":"From a plotting standpoint it's an interesting question- what sort of situation requires leaving the entire Milky Way and its hundred billion stars of potential behind? Divis Mal realizes he forgot something important and comes back for it? Some quantum-using species that's been living near the Schwarzchild radius of the central black hole in the Milky Way accidentally blows the whole thing up? Other than simple research curiosity, it would seem that something <i>big</i> is in the works if you have to go out that far, probably far bigger than the Doyen problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T21:24:00-07:00","id":1456926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhiannon Vashti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1456810-intergalactic-travel#post1456810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TC: \u00c6on says that intergalactic travel is currently not feasible. But what about satellite galaxies of the Milky Way such as the Magellanic Clouds or the Canis Major Dwarf? At least four of the Milky Way's satellites (the Sagittarius Dwarf Elliptical Galaxy, the Canis Major Dwarf, Segue 1 and Tucana III) are closer to Earth than Chrome Prime is and that world is well within Earth's capabilities to reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! How did you figure that out? Is it in one of the books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T21:37:26-07:00","id":1456928,"title":"","content":"You see, there's this Galactic Barrier; and if you try to cross it, you develop overwhelming psychic powers and go ask megalomaniacal\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026wait; wrong universe. <br /> <br /> But it <i>is</i> possible that there's some sort of barrier surrounding the Milky Way galaxy that prevents teleporters from leaving it. It wouldn't be the first time that something like that was implemented in the Trinity Continuum setting. Just not on that scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T21:51:58-07:00","id":1456929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1456810-intergalactic-travel?p=1456926#post1456926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow! How did you figure that out? Is it in one of the books?</div> </div> </div> </div>The distance between Earth and Chrome Prime is given in &quot;Distant Worlds&quot;. It's 86,000 LY. The Wikipedia article on satellites of the Milky Way gives a list of its known satellites and their distances. That's how I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26999-rhiannon-vashti","name":"Rhiannon Vashti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26999_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T22:03:54-07:00","id":1456930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1456810-intergalactic-travel?p=1456928#post1456928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it <i>is</i> possible that there's some sort of barrier surrounding the Milky Way galaxy that prevents teleporters from leaving it. It wouldn't be the first time that something like that was implemented in the Trinity Continuum setting. Just not on that scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you were wondering what to do with Aberrant players who are hitting Quantum 9, that might be an adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T01:07:15-07:00","id":1456937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1456810-intergalactic-travel?p=1456930#post1456930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if you were wondering what to do with Aberrant players who are hitting Quantum 9, that might be an adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plot twist: As they learn after taking out the barrier, contrary to Earth's barrier, the galactic one was made to keep the menaces out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T10:37:26-07:00","id":1457339,"title":"","content":"After more research, I realise that the satellite galaxies of the Milky Way, even the Magellanic Clouds, have very low metallicity and are not worth visiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26999-rhiannon-vashti","name":"Rhiannon Vashti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26999_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}